---
import Explorer from "../components/Explorer";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Corpus graph - document citation index</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Public-document corpus turned into a queryable citation graph in Postgres. Entities, edges, traversal, shortest path, and byte-exact provenance."
    />
    <!-- favicons (generated by build_favicon_set) -->
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/favicon-16.png" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/favicon-32.png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
    <link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest" />
  </head>
  <body class="mx-auto max-w-[1600px] p-3">
    <header class="mb-3 border-b-2 border-[var(--color-ink)] pb-2">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
        <h1 class="text-[15px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.08em]">
          Corpus graph &mdash; document citation index
        </h1>
        <span class="text-[11px] text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
          POSTGRES 17.6 &middot; PGROUTING 3.4.1 &middot; POSTGREST
        </span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-1 max-w-[110ch] text-[12px] text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
        Seven public-domain US federal documents, extracted to text and indexed
        as a citation graph. Entities are NIST control ids, statutes, regulations
        and Public Law numbers; edges are co-citation within a 400-character
        window. Traversal is a recursive CTE; shortest path and components are
        pgrouting over the same ordinary edge table. No graph database.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!--
      client:load, not client:visible. The explorer IS the page - deferring
      hydration until scroll would leave an empty shell above the fold.
    -->
    <Explorer client:load />

    <footer
      class="mt-4 border-t border-[var(--color-hairline-strong)] pt-2 text-[11px] text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]"
    >
      <p>
        Extraction is deterministic: these documents carry their cross-references
        as explicit, grammatically fixed citations, so every entity and edge is
        verifiable against the source text with no model in the loop. That is a
        property of this corpus, not a general claim - open-domain entity
        extraction needs an LLM pass and a human review step.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
